-Parameterized Tests
-
-• Boundary values find most bugs: zero, one, limit, limit plus one
-• Parameterized tests run one body against a table of cases
-• Provide a companion object inside the test class
-
-     • This object should provide a method that will return a list of parameter sets for the different test runs
-     • Those parameter sets will be provided as constructor parameters to the class
-     • The @Test function inside the class should use the parameters to execute the code and make the
-
-        assertion(s)
-
-• Test data builders hide irrelevant fields and show only what matters
-• Name each case so a failure identifies the input
-
